    "title": "National Bridge Inspection Practice Leader",
    "description": "National Bridge Inspection Practice Leader \n          REMOTE \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nAre you a proven leader in bridge inspection with a passion for delivering safe, reliable infrastructure? Garver is seeking a National Bridge Inspection Practice Leader to lead and grow our bridge inspection practice. This role combines technical expertise with strategic leadership, offering the opportunity to lead and build a dynamic team, manage key client relationships, and oversee a portfolio of profitable inspection projects.\n\nAs the Bridge Inspection Practice Leader, you will set the operational and strategic direction for our inspection practice, ensuring excellence in project delivery while driving business development and team growth. Youll have the autonomy to run a business within a business, supported by Garvers resources and collaborative culture.\n\n \n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\tDevelop and execute a strategic plan for bridge inspection services.\n\tRecruit, mentor, and manage a high-performing inspection team.\n\tFoster collaboration across design, inspection, and specialized service teams.\n\tBuild and maintain strong client relationships with DOTs and municipalities.\n\tLead proposal development, interviews, and presentations.\n\tIdentify and pursue new opportunities for inspection and related services.\n\tOversee and manage bridge inspection projects to SNBI and state-specific standards.\n\tEnsure compliance with safety and quality standards.\n\tCoordinate field operations, including scheduling and resource allocation.\n\tServe as a technical advisor for inspections, load ratings, and rehabilitation projects.\n\tProvide guidance on inspection methodologies, reporting, and data management.\n\tSupport integration of advanced tools and technologies in inspection workflows.\n\n\n \n\nExperience Requirements \n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil engineering from an ABET-accredited program.\n\tProfessional Engineer (PE) license.\n\tCompletion of NHI Course No. 130055 (Safety Inspection of In-Service Bridges). And refresher course 130053\n\t10+ years of experience in bridge inspection, with at least 5 years in a leadership or project management role. Qualify as a Bridge Inspection program Manager\n\tStrong knowledge of SNBI standards, AASHTO guidelines, and DOT processes.\n\tExcellent communication and leadership skills, with a proven ability to develop and manage teams.\n\tExperience preparing scopes, budgets, and schedules for inspection projects.\n\n\n \n\nPreferred Skills and Experience \n\n\n\tNHI Courses: 130078 (Bridge Inspection Techniques for Nonredundant Steel Tension Members (NSTM)), 130091 (Underwater Bridge Inspection).\n\tExperience with InspectX, AssetWise, AASHTOWare Bridge Management (BrM), and MicroStation.\n\tFamiliarity with asset management software and 3D modeling tools.\n\tPrevious experience leading inspection programs for DOTs or large municipalities.\n\tPerform load ratings and rehabilitation design using modern engineering tools and best practices.\n\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n \n\nLI-SM1",
