    "jobId": "8a7883a89029d31e01902d5eb5db2a1c",
    "title": "Quality Control (QC) - Sr. Process Engineer",
    "description": "Quality Control (QC) - Sr. Process Engineer \n          REMOTE \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nAre you an experienced Process Engineer interested extending your career by ensuring the quality of water and wastewater design with the best firm to work for in our industry?\n\nWeve got an opportunity for you on our Water Business Line (WBL) QC Team.\n\nAs part of Garvers WBL QC Team, you will be performing quality control reviews on designs for water and wastewater treatment facilities and other ancillary infrastructure associated with water and wastewater projects. Youll be reviewing process modeling, hydraulic modeling, design calculations, facility and equipment layouts, coordination with equipment vendors and coordination with regulatory agencies, and coordination with support disciplines and regional offices. You may travel occasionally, if desired, to coordinate with the design team.\n\nPerform QC review for:\n\n\n\tWater and wastewater treatment processes\n\tProcess modeling and develop criteria using analysis of water and wastewater process modeling data\n\tWater and wastewater process evaluation, selection, and implementation\n\tHydraulic analysis of water and wastewater treatment plants\n\tChemical storage and feed systems\n\tBlower systems and blower sizing\n\tProcess flow diagrams\n\tPiping and instrumentation diagrams\n\tSpecification and contract documents\n\n\nWhat youll bring:\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil, environmental, chemical, mechanical, or biosystems/agricultural engineering from an ABET accredited program\n\tMasters degree in civil, environmental, chemical, or related engineering discipline\n\t20 or more years of direct experience designing water and wastewater treatment facilities\n\tProfessional Engineer Licensure (PE)\n\tExperience with biological modeling software such as BioWin, GPS-X, and Sumo\n\tExperience working with a diverse disciplinary team, including civil, structural, building mechanical, electrical, and instrumentation and control (or I&C) disciplines\n\n\nBonus points if you bring these, too:\n\n\n\tExperience using Bluebeam software\n\tExperience with hydraulic modeling software such as Visual Hydraulics\n\n\nOur QC Team offers you the flexibility you have earned!\n\nThis position can be full-time with benefits or part-time on your schedule. These tasks can be performed remotely, in one of our design centers or regional offices, or some hybrid of both. Were looking for people who understand the work and understand work ethic. These positions report directly to the Quality Manager for Garvers WBL.\n\nBenefits & Perks\n\nGarvers committed to providing the best employee experience, and because we are a firm made up of engineers and designers who love data, we made that commitment measurable. Every year we ensure our benefits remain in the top quartile of our industry. What does that mean for you? Paid parental leave, 401k match, contributions to your HSA, paid health and dental insurance premiums for employees enrolled in our nationally recognized Wellness Program, gym membership reimbursements, tuition reimbursements, and much, much more.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGrow With Us \n\n\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance. \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,300 employees, Garver has a people-first culture that drives innovative, client-first service and is consistently recognized as a best firm to work for by Zweig Group. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com.  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law. \n\n\n\n\n \n\nLI-ED1",
