    "jobId": "8a7883ac9f8b941b019fb9a5ac78365f",
    "title": "Aviation Project Engineer (Entry Level)",
    "description": "Aviation Project Engineer (Entry Level) \n          Fayetteville, Arkansas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Garvers team of experienced professionals go beyond the basics to find innovative solutions that unlock future potential. The Garver Aviation Design Center in Fayetteville, AR, is looking for its next innovative Aviation Project Engineer. This individual will primarily be responsible for designing airport projects, including improvements to runways, taxiways, aprons, hangars, fuel farms, parking areas, terminal buildings, and other airport construction-related projects. \n\nFor the last six decades, Garver has designed aviation projects for more than 250 airport clients. Through this experience, Garver understands the complexities of airport systems held together by runways, roadways, facilities, and electrical systems that must work in tandem to accommodate daily needs for passenger travel and cargo transport. As part of Garvers commitment to continued innovation in airport design, our Aviation Design Center maintains a diverse, skilled design team dedicated to providing the expertise and leadership to assist our clients in meeting current and future needs. \n\nThe Aviation Project Engineer must be detail-oriented with solid self-initiative. They must be able to work as a member of a multi-disciplined team, work with diverse clients, and produce complete design phase deliverables, including drawings, specifications, cost estimates, exhibits, technical reports, and narratives. Creating construction documents includes drafting, quantity computations, specifications, and cost estimates. Design development software packages, including AutoCAD, Civil 3D, and other civil design packages, will be used. \n\nResponsibilities will include: \n\n\n\tDevelop technical deliverables under the guidance of senior engineers.  Technical deliverables include, but are not limited to: Construction Plans, Specifications, Design Reports, Permit Documents, and Cost Estimates. \n\tAttend and document client kick-off and progress review meetings. \n\tCoordinate with clients on project requirements and status updates. \n\tCoordinate with regulatory agencies to understand local permitting requirements and submit permit documents for review and approval. \n\tPerform construction administration duties including attending and documenting weekly construction meetings, conducting periodic site visits, reviewing shop drawings, and assisting with the development of change order, closeout, and other construction documentation.   \n\tPerform onsite construction observation and inspection. \n\n\nRequirements: \n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil engineering from an ABET-accredited program \n\t0-1 years of related experience \n\tPassed the FE exam, or ability to do so within 6 months of hire \n\tStrong written and oral communication skills with both internal employees and external clients \n\tSome travel may be required (approximately 10% with occasional overnight) \n\n\nPreferred Skills: \n\n \n\n\n\tStrong working knowledge and ability to design in CAD programs, including AutoCAD Civil 3D \n\n\nGrow with Us  \nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.   \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work for Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.",
    "jobUrl": "https://garverusa.com/careers/jobdescription/Aviation/Arkansas/Fayetteville/Aviation%20Project%20Engineer%20%28Entry%20Level%29/?gnk=job&gni=8a7883ac9f8b941b019fb9a5ac78365f&d=detail",
