    "jobId": "8a7887a89f38c239019f4312c0c6239e",
    "title": "Events and Tradeshows Planner",
    "description": "Events and Tradeshows Planner \n          Little Rock, Arkansas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            The Garver Communications Team is a group of strategic thinkers and creative doers all steadfastly focused on telling the story we live out every workday  that Garver is the best firm to work for and with. We do this by bringing on the best talent in our respective disciplines and collaborating in a fun, fast-paced environment to execute award-winning creative campaigns.\n\nWere looking to add an Events and Tradeshows Planner to our crew. With the support of a fully equipped creative team, you will assist internal clients in the promotion of tradeshow exhibitions and industry conferences, as well as project manage internal events that span Garvers 23-state footprint.\n\nIn this role, youll develop strategic promotions around some of Garvers most visible client and industry interactions: tradeshows and conferences. This highly organized individual will become a trusted advisor to our internal clients by bringing creativity, energy, and efficiency to Garvers presence at these events, while managing the many details it takes to execute them exactly. Youll also manage logistics for some internal events, communicating with employees across Garver Nation to ensure they get the most out of their experience. Occasional travel may be required.\n\n\nWhat Youll Do:\n\n\n\tEstablish relationships with our internal clients and develop promotion plans that most effectively meet their needs. \n\tServe as project manager to facilitate communications, creative, and collateral for 90+ conferences and trade shows per year. \n\tCollaborate with our designers, copywriters, photographers, videographers, and digital team members to take creative deliverables from concept to final product, including:\n\tPre-event emails\n\tCustomized printed collateral\n\tSocial media (promotion of conference presentations, presence at conference)\n\tEvents pages on GarverUSA.com\n\tCoordination of booth displays and graphics\n\tTradeshow advertising\n\tPromotion of giveaways\n\tSignage\n\tPromo items and apparel\n\tMaintain frequent touchpoints with your clients throughout the conference season\n\tManage promotion of and logistics for annual companywide events, specifically our executive teams annual Town Hall Tour and our Best Firm Celebrations.\n\n\n\nWhat Youll Bring:\n\n\n\tYou have at least five years of experience working as a project manager, preferably with coordinating events, meetings, and/or tradeshows.\n\tYou love to work with your clients and help them think creatively about how to best represent the Garver brand.\n\tYou have strong organizational skills and a keen attention to detail.\n\tYou think through and prioritize the audience experience: whether through digital communications or in person events.\n\tYoure structured, disciplined, and can manage multiple projects simultaneously.\n\tYoure stimulated by challenges.\n\tYou think on your feet every day, and pivot and multitask fluidly.\n\tBonus points if you have experience working with Asana or a similar project management system.\n\n\n \n\nGrow With Us\n \n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\nLI-CS1",
