    "title": "Senior Scheduler",
    "description": "Senior Scheduler \n          Fayetteville, Arkansas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Garver is looking to add a Senior Project Scheduler to our growing company with our Enterprise Solutions Scheduling Services Team. Overall, this position will be responsible for developing, reviewing, and maintaining critical path schedules for multiple projects.\n\n \n\nThis position will utilize broad knowledge and skills in a specific practice area, evaluate, select, and apply standard techniques, procedures, and criteria to perform a task or sequence of tasks for conventional projects with few complex features, collaboratively uses judgement to determine adaptations in methods for non-routine aspects of assignments, and lead limited teams for small projects as well as portions of large projects.\n\n \n\nThe Senior Scheduler is a critical position for our growing team and will be the lead or subject matter expert in at least one of these core competency areas: scheduling, estimating, or cost engineering.\n\n \n\nOther responsibilities will include but are not limited to:\n\n\n\tExpertise in Project Controls Methodologies\n\tLead development of periodic project controls reporting\n\tLead or direct the set up and reviews of the project controls status (i.e. cost contract, WBS, schedule, resources, etc.)\n\tLeading scheduling efforts on large and/or multiple projects\n\tDeveloping baseline schedules\n\tOverseeing schedule development/maintenance\n\tSupporting claims evaluation/mitigation issues\n\tContacting/following-up with project teams\n\tLeading training for project teams\n\tMonitoring compliance/reports non-compliance\n\tReporting scheduling metrics/risk issues\n\tDeveloping scheduling materials for proposals\n\tMentoring Schedulers/Junior Schedulers\n\tAssist in Developing scheduling materials for proposals. \n\tAbility to resolve scheduling issues that occur.\n\tProficient understanding of contract documents and the ability to learn to read and understand plans.\n\n\nThe successful candidate will be able to demonstrate through work experience their technical, subject matter expert, support position understanding and application of complex project controls principles.\n\n \n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, a comprehensive wellness program and Corporate Wellness Coordinator Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance. \n\n \n\nRequirements:\n\n\n\tHigh school diploma or equivalent\n\t10+ years of experience with project scheduling\n\tProficient knowledge of EPPM and various other scheduling software, including becoming proficient in web versions.\n\tExpert user of Primavera scheduling software (P6) and Microsoft Projects scheduling software\n\tComputer knowledge and efficiency, including Microsoft Office products\n\tExcellent written and verbal communication skills\n\tWilling to work flexible hours\n\tWilling to travel up to 10% of the time\n\n\nPreferred Skills:     \n\n\n\tAssociates degree in construction technology or construction management\n\tExperience in the construction and contracting industry standards\n\tThorough knowledge of construction sequencing\n\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n \n\nLI-SM1",
