    "jobId": "8a7883a89e6b0bf7019eb35649f40572",
    "title": "Project Surveyor",
    "description": "Project Surveyor \n          Rogers, Arkansas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nGarver, an ENR Top 500 engineering firm, seeks an engineering Project Surveyor in our Rogers, AR office for assistance on a variety of projects. Responsibilities will also involve processing field crew data, assistance with document reproduction for acquisitions, and quantity computations with guidance and supervision.\n\n \n\nThis position would work in the office creating vertical and horizontal control surveys networks, photogrammetry surveys, survey maps, 3D scanning models, plats and legal descriptions as well as processing and creating deliverables with state of the art surveying equipment such as Trimble GPS, total stations, digital levels, robotic equipment, 3-D scanning and S.L.A.M. equipment, and UAS LiDAR and Photogrammetry systems. In addition, the Project Surveyor will be available for CAD support for all Garver Survey projects.\n\n \n\nThis position will work alongside experienced design engineers, professional land surveyors, technicians, and project managers, in a high-performing and professional work environment.\n\n \n\nOur Construction and Survey Services Team offers a fast-paced, highly collaborative work environment with the opportunity to gain direct hands-on experience. A successful candidate will be required to meet the following physical demands that are essential to the job:\n\n\n\tRegularly stand and/or walk while holding tools or objects in the field\n\tReach with hands and arms; stoop, kneel, and crouch\n\tRegularly lift/move up to 25 pounds, frequently lift/move up to 10 pounds, and occasionally lift/move up to 50 pounds\n\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\t2+ years of survey experience and/or an AS or BS degree focused on Survey Sciences\n\tKnowledge of Survey principles and practices\n\tWillingness to work alone or with an experienced surveyor\n\tWillingness to travel 10% of the time\n\tEffective written and verbal communication skills      \n\tStrong organizational skills and attention to detail\n\n\nPreferred Skills\n\n\n\tPLS licensure\n\tExperience with various DOT standards\n\tCivil 3D and/or OpenRoads experience\n\tTransportation/Roadway engineering plan production experience\n\tExperience working with Engineering staff and maintaining plan production standards\n\tProficiency with Trimble equipment and software\n\tExperience with UAS surveys and workflows\n\tExperience extracting Lidar data\n\tOpen to more experienced candidates\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n \n\nLI-VR1",
