    "jobId": "8a7887ac9d02e529019d301dec98788c",
    "title": "Structural Designer",
    "description": "Structural Designer \n          Fayetteville, Arkansas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            As a member of our growing Water Design team, the Structural Designer will be responsible for developing and detailing Revit 3D models and construction drawings for water and wastewater facilities projects. This role collaborates closely with structural engineers and multidisciplinary teams to support the design and delivery of treatment plants, pump stations, and related facilities.\n\n \n\nThis role in the Water Design Center is one that is central to project delivery through our many offices and utilizes the latest BIM technology, predominantly Revit software to produce high-quality structural models and drawings. Typical projects include reinforced concrete basins, tanks, process structures, equipment foundations, and building structures within water and wastewater treatment facilities. for water and wastewater treatment plants.\n\n \n\nPrimary responsibilities of the Structural Designer will include:\n\n\n\tDevelop and maintain structural Revit 3D models with moderate to high autonomy\n\tPrepare plans, sections, and detailed structural drawings for concrete, steel, and masonry systems\n\tAssist in model coordination and clash detection using BIM tools\n\tProduce construction documents in coordination with engineers and project teams\n\tIncorporate field data, redlines, and as-built information into models and drawings\n\tWorking as team player with a group of technicians and designers of various levels and disciplines (process, structural, mechanical, and electrical) along with Project Leaders and design teams to execute projects and developed detailed design drawings.\n\tArranging necessary resources for file sharing and communication to effectively share design files across the company or with clients, sub consultants, and contractors;\n\tMaintaining strong communication with engineers and project managers to ensure timely delivery of projects and avoid any potential project conflicts\n\tQuality program compliance, including QA/QC to ensure all projects adhere to company standards\n\n\nDue to the collaborative nature of coordination using BIM tools, candidates must have the ability to seek out and resolve issues through close interaction with other project team members.  In addition, the candidate must be able to maintain a positive team attitude and interpersonal effectiveness to foster and maintain an efficient and productive team. \n\n \n\n\nAbout Garvers Water Design Center:\n\n \n\nThe Water Design Center (WDC) is a knowledge-based hub that excels in highly technical, multi-discipline water and wastewater designs. The WDC specializes in large, high-volume, custom treatment plant projects with advanced technologies. Centralizing the location of the WDC means communication, coordination, and participation with team members is constant. This integral working relationship benefits the client through project delivery schedule and design quality, as well as opportunity for team collaboration and professional growth.\n\n\n \n\nRequirements:\n\n\n\tAssociates or Bachelors degree in CAD, BIM, Engineering Technology, or related field\n\t5+ years of structural drafting/design experience (water/wastewater preferred)\n\tProficiency in Autodesk Revit (required); AutoCAD experience is a plus\n\tExperience with reinforced concrete, masonry building, and structural steel detailing\n\tStrong understanding of structural construction drawings and structural systems \n\tAbility to manage multiple tasks and meet project deadlines\n\n\nPreferred Skills: \n\n\n\tUnderstanding of water or wastewater treatment specific structural design\n\tExperience using Bluebeam software\n\tExperience with file sharing protocols and other methods of file transfer\n\tGood communication and training skills (verbal and written)\n\tAssociate degree or higher with a focus on CAD/BIM\n\tExperience with Autodesk Construction Cloud and BIM360 file sharing software\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\n\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n\n \n\nLI-RK1",
