    "jobId": "8a78839f974d4cb10197a28592c22d19",
    "title": "Aviation Design Manager",
    "description": "Aviation Design Manager \n          Denver, Colorado \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            For the last six decades, Garver has been designing projects for more than 250 aviation clients. Through this experience, Garver understands the complexities of airport systems held together by runways, roadways, facilities, and electrical systems that need to work in tandem to accommodate daily needs for travel and transport. As part of Garvers commitment to continued innovation in airport design, our Aviation team maintains a diverse, skilled design team dedicated to providing the expertise and leadership to assist our clients in meeting both current and future needs.\n\n \n\nDo you enjoy creating innovative, creative, and forward-thinking conceptual designs for airport improvements? Do you enjoy positively impacting public works through civil infrastructure projects? Do you enjoy making complex design ideas accessible to the public? Our Aviation team is looking for a Aviation Design Manager to help create design solutions for our aviation clients.\n\n \n\nAs part of the Aviation team for Garver, this Aviation Design Manager will have an opportunity to develop and edit conceptual design deliverables in support of various projects across the United States. Diversity in high-volume, large scale aviation projects will allow the candidate to be directly engaged in the production of marketing and design phase deliverables including detailed project approaches, technical reports, specifications or narratives, and document assembly.  \n\n \n\nWhat youll do:\n\nGenerally, the responsibilities of this role will entail working with several different teams of mostly engineers to develop conceptual designs for marketing pursuits collaborate with a multi-disciplined staff in the creation of marketing materials, and technical reports for various types of projects including terminal programs, airfield pavements, hangar facilities, electrical NAVAIDs, and aviation planning.  The ideal candidate would experience with aviation design for both commercial and general aviation airports, as well as the ability to provide outstanding service to internal clients.\n\n \n\nDay to day responsibilities will include, but are not limited to:\n\n\n\tProject Management of conceptual designs for proposals\n\tCoordinate efforts from technicians and technical writers to support of deliverables.  \n\tCreation and collaboration on airport designs.\n\tWork with Project Managers and Engineers to incorporate the appropriate level of detail in each deliverable\n\tParticipate in project progress meetings\n\n\nSome occasional travel may be required for industry related conference attendance or project specific meetings. Due to the collaborative nature of coordination for large infrastructure projects, candidates must have the ability to seek out and resolve issues through close interaction with other project team members.  In addition, the candidate should be able to maintain a positive team attitude and interpersonal effectiveness to work within a team environment. \n\n \n\nProjected Compensation Range $108,600 to $165,800\n\n(salary range considers differences in incentive compensation commensurate with qualifications, experience, and performance)\n\n\nApplications are accepted on an ongoing basis; there is currently no fixed application deadline.\n\n\n \n\nGarver Benefits Offered:\n\n\n\tFree individual health coverage with dental benefits\n\tFamily health care coverage options\n\tHealthcare savings and flexible spending accounts\n\tFlexible work schedules and opportunities to work remotely\n\tPaid parental leave and adoption assistance\n\t401(k) matching\n\tIn-house Wellness Team and on-site fitness centers\n\tReimbursement for gym fees and other health-related services\n\tEarn Wellness rewards (up to $500 each year!)\n\tHealth coaching services\n\tIn-house professional development program\n\tCompany-paid professional memberships and industry licenses\n\tTuition reimbursement program\n\tEmployee recognition awards\n\tEmployee Referral bonus program that offers incentives up to $10,000!\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n \n\nLI-VR1",
