    "jobId": "8a78859f9db1e91b019db68e359d45f4",
    "title": "Aviation Construction Manager",
    "description": "Aviation Construction Manager \n          Denver, Colorado \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nGarver is seeking a talented Aviation Construction Manager to join our growing Aviation in Denver. This role is ideal for a dynamic professional who thrives in a fast-paced environment and is passionate about delivering high-impact projects for airline clients.\n\n \n\nAs a (Construction Manager), youll lead Owners Rep, Construction, and Airline-related projects, supporting a wide range of aviation planning and client management services. Youll collaborate directly with airlines and airport stakeholders to ensure projects are delivered on time, within budget, and to the highest standards.\n\n \n\nWhat Youll Do:\n\n\n\tSupport design and construction administration for one or multiple aviation clients.\n\tManage contracts, change orders, and project documentation.\n\tConduct site walkthroughs and track contractor progress.\n\tCoordinate schedules, budgets, and logistics across project phases.\n\tPrepare client deliverables including reports, memos, and briefings.\n\tAttend pre-qualification and bid evaluation processes.\n\n\nWhat Were Looking For:\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in Aviation, Architecture, Construction, Engineering, or related field.\n\t5+ years of experience in airport or commercial construction projects.\n\tStrong communication and organizational skills.\n\tProficiency in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Power BI).\n\tWillingness to travel (up to 10%) with occasional overnight stays.\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n\n\tExperience working directly with airports, airport operations, or airlines.\n\tFamiliarity with project/construction management platforms.\n\tAviation-related experience (e.g., licensed pilot).\n\tDelivery of construction project under alternative delivery methods (CMAR, DB, PDB, etc.)\n\n\n\nProjected Compensation Range $110,000 to $155,000\n\n(salary range considers differences in incentive compensation commensurate with qualifications, experience, and performance)\n\nApplications are anticipated to close on October 1, 2026, but may be extended based on business needs.\n\n\n \n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\nLI-VR1",
