    "jobId": "8a78859f9db1e91b019db6935f664838",
    "title": "Construction Inspector",
    "description": "Construction Inspector \n          Denver, Colorado \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nGarver has an opening in our Denver office for a Construction Inspector whose primary duties will include the inspection and observation of airport heavy civil construction projects. \n\n \n\nThis position will be responsible for observing, inspecting, and documenting construction activities and will be under the supervision of the Project Engineer or Manager assigned to a specific project. This position will assist the Project Engineers and Project Managers as needed to ensure that the project is built in accordance with project plans and specifications under which the contract was awarded. \n\nPrimary responsibilities of this role include but are not limited to:\n\n\n\tActing as the agent of the Owner to ensure that the installation of the work meets or exceeds the plans and specifications\n\tInteracting with staff, contractors, airport and airline staff, the public, and others encountered in the course of work\n\tRegular use of written and oral communication skills\n\tReading and interpreting data, information, and documents\n\tAnalyzing and solving problems\n\tObserving and interpreting situations on construction job sites\n\tPerforming highly detailed work on multiple, concurrent tasks\n\tWorking under intensive deadlines\n\tWorking with the Contractor to facilitate production and to actively engage in problem solutions when problems do present on the project site\n\tReviewing quantities in pay applications on a monthly basis to ensure that the Contractor is billing accurately\n\n\nApplicants must be capable of considerable physical activity in an outdoor setting including but not limited to light lifting, bending, stooping and climbing, walking and standing for prolonged periods of time, and regularly operating motorized vehicles. All applicants must consent to a background check, drug screen, motor vehicle report as a requirement of employment.\n\n \n\nRequirements:\n\n\n\t10 or more years of experience in construction inspections, surveying or materials testing and inspection\n\tHigh school diploma or equivalent\n\tComputer and electronic filing of documents using various PMIS Systems.  (Procore, E-Builder, Autodesk, etc.)\n\tValid Drivers License\n\n\nPreferred Skills:\n\n\n\tPrior heavy civil, airport experience (whether as a contractor or as an inspector/Owners agent)\n\tSurveying or materials testing and inspection experience\n\tCoursework in Construction Management\n\tCertified Concrete Technician (ACI Certification)\n\tOSHA 10/30 certifications and other industry specific training and/or certifications\n\tOther testing and inspection certifications\n\n\n \n\n\nProjected Compensation Range $62,000 to $90,000\n\n(salary range considers differences in incentive compensation commensurate with qualifications, experience, and performance)\n\nApplications are anticipated to close on October 1, 2026, but may be extended based on business needs.\n\n \n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n \n\nLI-VR1",
