    "jobId": "8a78859f9c72dc92019c8b7a0e2f7445",
    "title": "Transportation Team Leader",
    "description": "Transportation Team Leader \n          Tampa, Florida \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Join our team at Garver, an award-winning national full-service firm. We pride ourselves on our unique organizational structure that empowers local decision-making, ensuring swift adaptation to evolving needs. With a distinctive combination of nationwide resources, local autonomy, and the expertise of seasoned Subject Matter Experts (SMEs), we invest in our employees so they can excel in delivering unparalleled service to our clients and communities. At Garver, youll enjoy a collaborative team environment, with ample opportunities for both professional mastery and autonomy in your work. Join us in making a difference!\n\n\nGarver is seeking a Transportation Team Leader to oversee client relationships and manage projects as part of our growing team in the Tampa area. They will be mentored and trained as seller-doers with opportunities to lead projects, market our services, interact with the biggest transportation clients in Florida, and perform the work.\n \nResponsibilities:\n             Client interaction and business development\n             Project management\n             Sub-consultant coordination\n             Project/task scheduling\n             Knowledge of transportation design\n             Team oversight\n \nTechnical experience should include:\n             Geometric design for roadways/interchanges\n             Construction sequencing and traffic control\n             Utility relocation coordination\n             Marketing activities may include assisting in the production of proposals and letters of interest, as well as participation in interviews and other presentations.\n\n\nRequirements:\n             Bachelors degree in civil engineering from an ABET accredited program\n             Licensed as a Professional Engineer (PE) in the State of Florida, or will have the ability to obtain reciprocity within three months of hire\n             Ten (10) or more years of relevant experience\n             Practical working knowledge of the American Association of State Highway and Transportation Officials (AASHTO) Green Book and the Manual Uniform Traffic Control Device (MUTCD) as well as FDOT Design manuals and processes\n             Strong written and verbal communication skills\n             Strong working knowledge of MS Office\n \nPreferred Skills:\n             Previous experience in consulting engineering with a primary focus on DOT transportation projects\n \nGrow With Us\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n \nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com.\n \nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n \nLI-SM1",
