    "jobId": "8a7883a89f8b945d019fce9552aa7d38",
    "title": "Senior Water/Wastewater Project Manager",
    "description": "Senior Water/Wastewater Project Manager \n          Tampa, Florida \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nGarver is seeking a Senior Water/Wastewater Project Manager to join our growing Water team in Tampa, Florida. This position offers an opportunity to play a key role in expanding Garvers municipal water and wastewater practice throughout Tampa Bay and Florida.\n\n \n\nWorking closely with the Tampa Water Business Team Leader, the successful candidate will lead \n\nmultidisciplinary infrastructure projects, serve as a trusted advisor to municipal clients, lead and support strategic pursuits, and mentor developing project managers and technical staff. The candidate will be supported by Garvers national network of water, wastewater, conveyance, treatment, and alternative-delivery professionals while helping build a strong local team.\n\n \n\nThis position is based in Garvers Tampa office, offers flexibility consistent with Garver policy, and requires periodic travel throughout Florida for client meetings, project needs, and industry events.\n\n \n\nRepresentative Projects\n\n\n\tWastewater pump stations, lift stations, and force mains\n\tWater booster and repump stations, transmission mains, and storage facilities\n\tWastewater collection and water distribution system rehabilitation\n\tWater, wastewater, and reclaimed-water treatment improvements\n\tUtility master planning, condition assessment, and hydraulic modeling\n\tEqualization, wet-weather, resiliency, and system-consolidation projects\n\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n\n\tServe as project manager and primary client contact for municipal water and wastewater assignments.\n\tManage project scope, schedule, budget, staffing, quality, risk, invoicing, forecasting, change management, and overall financial performance.\n\tDevelop and maintain trusted relationships with municipal utility clients throughout Tampa Bay and Florida.\n\tIdentify project opportunities and lead pursuit strategy, proposals, interviews, scope and fee development, and contract negotiations in coordination with Water Business Line leadership.\n\tLead multidisciplinary teams through planning, design, permitting, bidding, construction, startup, and closeout.\n\tCoordinate technical specialists, support disciplines, subconsultants, and construction-phase personnel while remaining accountable for overall project quality.\n\tFacilitate client, stakeholder, and technical workshops and communicate project status, decisions, risks, and required actions clearly.\n\tMentor project managers and engineers and assist with recruiting and development of the Tampa Water team.\n\tParticipate in relevant professional and industry organizations and represent Garver in the Florida water market.\n\n\nRequired Qualifications\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil, environmental, chemical, or a related engineering discipline from an ABET-accredited program.\n\tAt least 12 years of progressively responsible municipal water and wastewater engineering or consulting experience.\n\tAt least five years of successful project management experience, including responsibility for scope, schedule, budget, quality, financial performance, and client satisfaction.\n\tLicensed as a Professional Engineer in Florida, or able to obtain Florida licensure by endorsement within six months of employment.\n\tExperience managing multidisciplinary water or wastewater infrastructure projects through design and construction.\n\tDemonstrated ability to develop scopes, fees, schedules, staffing plans, and project delivery strategies.\n\tStrong written, verbal, client-service, negotiation, and team-leadership skills.\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n\n\tEstablished professional relationships within the Tampa Bay or broader Florida municipal utility market.\n\tExperience leading proposals and interviews for publicly procured professional services.\n\tExperience managing pump station, pipeline, storage, treatment, rehabilitation, or utility-planning projects.\n\tExperience with collaborative delivery methods such as CMAR, design-build, or progressive design-build.\n\tDemonstrated success mentoring staff and developing project management talent.\n\tRelevant professional credentials, such as DBIA, PMP, or ENV SP, and active participation in organizations such as AWWA or WEF.\n\n\n\nWorking Conditions\n\nGenerally works in an office setting. Occasional travel to offsite locations to perform work and work-related tasks or attend meetings may be required. Physical demands include the ability to hear, understand, and distinguish speech in-person and on the phone, and visual acuity to read printed materials and screens. Must be able to operate standard office equipment. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.\n\n \n\nThis job description is intended to be generic in nature and may not include all assigned duties and responsibilities.\n\n\n\n\nGrow With Us \n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance. \n\n\n\n  \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver has a people-first culture that drives innovative, client-first service and is consistently recognized as a best firm to work for by Zweig Group. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com.  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law. \n\nLI-ED1",
