    "jobId": "8a78859f9fd3baa0019fee8556392672",
    "title": "Finance Billing Specialist",
    "description": "Finance Billing Specialist \n          Wichita, Kansas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Garver is seeking a professional, motivated individual to join our Finance Team. This position will offer an array of responsibilities while supporting Garvers Project Managers and the Finance Team.\n\n \n\nResponsibilities of this Finance Billing Specialist will include, but are not limited to:\n\n\n\tWorking directly with Project Managers to set up projects and budgets according to contract specifications\n\tMaintaining accurate records within ERP for project details, budgets, and invoices\n\tGeneration of monthly billing packets for Project Manager review\n\tClient billing\n\tMaintain documentation of client related procedures, deadlines, and other guidelines\n\tMaintain documentation of Project Manager preferences related to billing\n\tEfficient management and recordkeeping of monthly project reports\n\tProvide financial reporting upon Project Managers request\n\tPro-actively monitor AR and WIP aging and address them with assigned Project Managers\n\tCollaborating with other Garver technical leaders or Finance staff for special projects as needed\n\tAiding other Finance Team members as requested\n\tAll other related duties as assigned\n\n\nRequirements:\n\n\n\t3-5 years of billing or accounting experience\n\tProficient in Microsoft Excel and Word\n\tStrong mathematical, written, and verbal communication skills\n\tProblem solver and highly driven\n\tProven experience in utilizing ERP systems or specialized billing software\n\n\nThe successful candidate will have the ability to work on projects independently and collaboratively. They must have a service-minded approach, confidence in decision-making, and proven experience in effective time-management. For the right candidate, this role could open the door to further growth potential within Garvers Finance Team.\n\n \n\nAll interested candidates are encouraged to submit a cover letter with their application stating how their experience and skills would make them a potential fit for this role.\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\nGrow With Us \n\n\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance. \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,300 employees, Garver has a people-first culture that drives innovative, client-first service and is consistently recognized as a best firm to work for by Zweig Group. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com.  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law. \n\n\n\n\n \n\nLI-CS1",
