    "jobId": "8a7883ac9efb8722019f3e9259975003",
    "title": "CAD Technician",
    "description": "CAD Technician \n          Wichita, Kansas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Garvers Transportation team, an integrated group with deep expertise in bridge and structural engineering, is seeking a CAD Technician to join our growing team. This candidate will assist in the drafting and design of construction documents on a variety of municipal and civil transportation projects. \n\n \n\nAdditional assignments may involve processing field data, organizing drawing and file structure, conceptual/preliminary alignment layouts, preparing 3D models with engineers, quantity computations and cost estimates with guidance and supervision.  The CAD Technician will be an integral part of setting and maintaining standards, developing tools, quality program compliance, including delivery of quality work as part of Garvers high standards.  \n\n \n\nRequirements\n\n\n\tA Technical school certificate or an associate degree or higher in drafting, design surveying, GIS or combination of relevant coursework and drafting experience\n\tUnderstanding and application of drafting methods, standards, and procedures\n\tWorking knowledge of MicroStation drafting and design software\n\tWorking knowledge Civil 3D\n\tWorking knowledge of Bluebeam or other PDF editor\n\tEffective written and communication skills\n\tAbility to work effectively with a mentor and as part of a team\n\n\nPreferred Skills\n\n\n\tExperience with MicroStation Geopak SS10 and/or OpenRoads Designer\n\t5 plus years of related drafting experience in Transportation projects\n\n\n \n\nGrow With Us\n\n\n\n\n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n\n\n \n\nLI-SM1",
