    "jobId": "8a7887a1902d7832019099dfbd39445d",
    "title": "Water Facilities Team Lead",
    "description": "Water Facilities Team Lead \n          Overland Park, Kansas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nGarver is seeking a Water Facilities Team Leader in Overland Park, KS to build and maintain a portfolio of profitable water / wastewater projects. The projects consist of the study, planning, design, and implementation of treatment facilities for Water and Wastewater. This senior leadership position provides the opportunity for someone to grow their own team and business portfolio, with autonomy to focus on the growth of revenues and production for a set of clients of their choosing. \n\n \n\nProject responsibilities may include planning, design, and managing a variety of projects related to water and wastewater treatment facilities. The Water Facilities Team Leader will work closely with Garvers Overland Park Water Business Team Leader to grow our practice. This position presents an opportunity for significant career advancement and industry-wide recognition through an entrepreneurial approach to creating what we believe Kansas clients will soon view as the best firm to work with.\n\n \n\nThe successful Water Facilities Team Leader must be proficient in the following skills:\n\n\n\tTeam Leadership: must assemble, develop, mentor, and oversee a highly motivated team.\n\tProject Management: must prepare scope-of-work and level-of-effort estimates for contract proposals; must lead and manage team for successful execution of contracted scope, budget, and schedule\n\tSenior Water / Wastewater Design Engineer: must be proficient at the execution of planning, design, bidding, and construction administration phases of water and wastewater infrastructure projects\n\tBusiness Development: must develop, capture, and maintain workload for the team throughout Kansas, by establishing and maintaining positive relationships with clients.\n\tClient Service Management: must develop and maintain a healthy network of clients throughout Kansas.\n\n\nThis role will offer the opportunity to leverage Garvers established, nationally respected Water Services Team and concentrated, industry experts to support business development initiatives for an up-and-coming firm in Kansas. Mentorship and development from seasoned leadership and peers will allow this Facilities Team Leader to have a direct impact on building Garvers legacy of providing outstanding engineering services to water and wastewater clients in Kansas.\n\n \n\nRequirements:\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil or environmental engineering from an ABET accredited program\n\tLicensed Professional Engineer in the state of Kansas\n\t8 or more years of similar experience in the water/wastewater utilities market with a focus on treatment\n\t5 or more years of project management experience\n\tWorking knowledge of presentation software such as MS PowerPoint or Keynote\n\tStrong communication skills and public speaking ability\n\n\nPreferred Skills:\n\n\n\tMasters degree in civil or environmental engineering from an ABET accredited program\n\t5 or more years of similar experience in supporting municipalities in Kansas\n\tExperience with state and or national conference technical presentations on water/wastewater treatment topics\n\tStrong existing client relationships with multiple Kansas municipal water and wastewater utilities\n\n\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n\n\n \n\nLI-ED1",
