    "jobId": "8a78859e9d4aea68019d6891aa3e665d",
    "title": "Municipal Project Engineer",
    "description": "Municipal Project Engineer \n          Ridgeland, Mississippi \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nGarver is seeking a Municipal Project Engineer to complement our reputable staff and join our growing Transportation Team in our Ridgeland, MS office to continue the tradition of providing quality service to our clients. \n\n \n\nResponsibilities of this position will be to assist in the design and creation of construction documents on a wide variety of projects including:\n\n\n\tLeading and assisting in the design and creation of construction documents on municipal transportation and drainage projects such as major thoroughfares, collectors, residential streets, and trails.\n\tRoadway design components including typical sections, geometric layouts, drainage and hydraulic analysis, erosion control plans, pedestrian mobility and safety features, maintenance of traffic plans, and storm water quality plans.\n\tAssignments will also involve tasks associated with leading or producing a set of construction documents including design, drafting, quantity computations, specifications, cost estimates, client coordination and meetings, and coordination with subconsultants.\n\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\tBachelors Degree in Civil Engineering from an ABET accredited program\n\tHave passed the Fundamentals of Engineering (FE) exam\n\t4-10 years of related experience\n\tStrong communication skills\n\tHave design software training\n\n\nPreferred Skills\n\n\n\tLicensed as a Professional Engineer (PE) in the state of Mississippi.\n\tExperience in municipal design, specifically horizontal and vertical geometrics. Roadway drainage design and storm sewer design experience is a plus.\n\tExperience with Municipal or DOT roadway designs including the development of new transportation elements, ADA/Pedestrian elements, proposed roadway profiles, and cross sections\n\tWorking knowledge of Autodesk Civil 3D, MicroStation or Open Roads Designer.\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n \n\nLI-SM1",
