    "jobId": "8a7887ac9a31eebd019a50eafa5757ee",
    "title": "Digital Built Environment Technician",
    "description": "Digital Built Environment Technician \n          Kansas City, Missouri \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nThe Digital Built Environment Technician will support the creation of accurate 3D models of existing facilities, primarily using Revit and point cloud data produced with various reality capture workflows. Working with our Buildings Business Line as part of our Digital Built Environment team, this role will focus on scan-to-BIM (as-built modeling) with a strong emphasis on MEPF systems in complex facilities such as hospitals, airports, educational facilities, etc.\n\n \n\nCollaborating closely with project managers, engineers, modelers, and scanning technicians, the ideal candidate will bring both technical precision and communication skills to ensure accurate modeling of existing conditions. This role is critical to the success of our reality capture and as-built modeling initiatives, leveraging the latest BIM and point cloud technologies.\n\n \n\nPrimary responsibilities will include:\n\n\n\tDevelop accurate and detailed 3D BIM models in Revit, based on point cloud data and existing building documentation.\n\tProduce high-quality drawing sets including plans, sections, elevations, and 3D details within Revit.\n\tProcess and interpret point cloud data (from sources such as LiDAR scanners and mobile mapping systems) to inform accurate as-built modeling.\n\tParticipate in clash detection efforts and assist in coordinating issue resolution between design teams, VDC teams, and construction stakeholders.\n\tCollaborate with multidisciplinary teams, including architectural, structural, and MEPF disciplines, to support both design and reality capture projects.\n\tPerform QA/QC checks to verify model accuracy, adherence to company BIM standards, and alignment with project-specific requirements.\n\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\tProficiency in Autodesk Revit for modeling and documentation of building systems.\n\tStrong organizational skills and attention to detail in both modeling and documentation.\n\tClear and professional communication skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across disciplines.\n\tFamiliarity with point cloud processing tools (e.g., ReCap, NavVis, or similar) and Scan-to-BIM workflows is preferred.\n\tExperience with MEPF modeling, construction documentation, or as-built modeling is a plus.\n\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n \n\nLI-CS1",
