    "description": "Municipal Project Manager \n          Kansas City, Missouri \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nJoin our team at Garver, an award-winning national full-service firm. We pride ourselves in delivering unparalleled services to our clients by collaborating with local decision makers and by ensuring innovative solutions and swift adaptation to the evolving needs of the communities. With a distinctive combination of nationwide resources, history of being a trusted advisor, local recognition, and the expertise of seasoned Subject Matter Experts, we invest in our employees so they can excel in delivering unparalleled service to our clients and communities. At Garver, youll enjoy a collaborative team environment, with ample opportunities for both professional mastery and upward growth. Join us in making a difference and lets build transportation solutions that will enhance our communities!\n\n \n\nGarver seeks a Municipal Project Manager to join our growing Transportation Team in Overland Park, KS or Kansas City, MO to continue the tradition of providing reputable service to our clients and adding to our award winning culture.\n\n \n\nResponsibilities of this role include:\n\n\n\tProject management\n\tSub-consultant coordination\n\tProject/task scheduling\n\tCivil Design\n\tPlan production oversight\n\tPreparing cost estimates\n\tQuality Control\n\tTraining other engineers\n\tClient relationship building\n\tTechnical experience should include:\n\t\n\t\tGeometric design for roadways/intersections\n\t\t3D Design experience\n\t\tDrainage design\n\t\tConstruction sequencing and traffic control\n\t\n\t\n\tMarketing activities may include assisting in the production of proposals, as well as participation in interviews and other presentations.\n\n\nRequirements:\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil engineering from an ABET accredited program\n\tLicensed as a Professional Engineer (PE) in the State of Missouri and Kansas, or will have the ability to obtain reciprocity\n\tMinimum of six (6) years of relevant experience\n\tPractical working knowledge of the American Association of State Highway and Transportation Officials (AASHTO) Green Book, the Roadside Design Guide, and the Manual Uniform Traffic Control Device (MUTCD)\n\tExperience with AutoCad Civil 3D, Microstation, OpenRoads Designer or InRoads and/or other roadway design software\n\tStrong written and verbal communication skills\n\tStrong working knowledge of MS Office\n\n\nPreferred Skills:\n\n\n\tPrevious experience in consulting engineering with a primary focus on Kansas City Metro and/or Missouri municipal clients\n\t3D Design experience\n\tUtility Relocation Coordination Experience\n\n\n Grow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.",
