    "jobId": "8a78859e9eb34c5b019ef530f4e919b0",
    "title": "Site Civil Project Engineer (Entry Level)",
    "description": "Site Civil Project Engineer (Entry Level) \n          Greenville, South Carolina \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \n\nAre you eager to kickstart your engineering career? At Garvers Water Design Center in Greenville, SC, we offer an exciting opportunity to immerse yourself in impactful projects and accelerate your professional development. As a Site Civil Project Engineer, youll gain hands-on experience in designing and optimizing essential water and wastewater systems, all while collaborating with experienced engineers from various fields who will mentor and guide you. This role is for motivated individuals who are ready to learn, contribute to significant projects, and build a solid foundation for a successful career in civil engineering.\n\n \n\nWhat Youll Do:\n\nAs a Site Civil Project Engineer, youll be involved in a variety of design tasks, including:\n\n\n\tDeveloping and optimizing conveyance systems for treatment plant processes\n\tCreating detailed site layouts, grading plans, and stormwater management designs\n\tDesigning site access, paving, and distribution systems, including piping and pump stations\n\tPlanning and evaluating collection systems, including interceptor and outfall piping\n\n\n \n\nWhy Garver?\n\nAt Garver, we offer a collaborative and forward-thinking environment where your growth is our priority. Youll work closely with senior engineers on diverse and exciting projects, gaining valuable experience and contributing to innovative solutions. Youll be focused on creating cost-effective designs for long-term operational efficiency while maintaining community and environmental responsibility.\n\n \n\nWhat Were Looking For:\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil engineering from an ABET-accredited program\n\t0-2 years experience in site civil design\n\tEngineer in Training (EIT), or ability to obtain registration within 6 months of hire\n\tStrong communication skills and proficiency in MS Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Outlook)\n\tA proactive, team-oriented approach and a genuine enthusiasm for engineering\n\n\n \n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n\n\tMasters degree in civil, environmental, or a related engineering discipline\n\tFamiliarity with Autodesk software, including AutoCAD and Revit\n\tExperience with site layout or land development, utility piping, grading, drainage systems, and exposure to water and wastewater facilities\n\tActive involvement in professional organizations\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\nGrow With Us\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n \nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n \nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.",
