    "jobId": "8a7885ac9f8b9423019f956da17d1066",
    "title": "Structural Engineer (Entry Level)",
    "description": "Structural Engineer (Entry Level) \n          Greenville, South Carolina \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Interested in developing structural designs for complex, large concrete water bearing structures? And for improvements to new and existing water and wastewater treatment facilities? Enjoy providing structural support for a variety of important water and wastewater projects? Want to make a difference in your community and beyond? \n\nWeve got an opportunity for you here at our Water Design Center (WDC) in Greenville, SC. \n\nAs part of Garvers growing WDC, youll be part of a project team producing structural designs for water and wastewater treatment facilities, pump stations, lift stations, and other ancillary infrastructure associated with water and wastewater projects. Youll be engaged in structural layout, design calculations, coordinating with other BIM structural designers, and performing quality reviews. Youll travel occasionally when a project requires a site assessment as well as support during construction. \n\nWhat youll do: \n\n\n\tProduce structural designs for clarifiers, process basins, filters, admin buildings, pump stations, lift stations, tanks, vaults, retaining walls, and other ancillary structures associated with water and wastewater infrastructure projects \n\tDevelop complex finite element models to analyze various structures. \n\tComplete structural design calculations for concrete, steel, aluminum, and masonry \n\tOversee the development of construction drawings and 3D models while coordinating between various disciplines \n\tPrepare construction cost estimates \n\tCoordinate with geotechnical subconsultants \n\tSupport construction projects by reviewing submittals and site visits \n\n\nWhat youll bring: \n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil or structural engineering from an ABET accredited program \n\t0-1 year structural design experience \n\tEngineer In Training (EIT) or ability to obtain a EIT registration within 6 months \n\tBasic understanding of structural engineering design with concrete, and structural steel \n\n\nBonus points if you bring these, too: \n\n\n\tMasters degree in civil or structural engineering \n\tUnderstanding of the structural complexities associated with water and wastewater treatment equipment \n\tFamiliarity with Autodesk Revit \n\tExperience using Bluebeam \n\tExperience working with a diverse disciplinary team, including process, civil, building mechanical, electrical, and instrumentation and control disciplines \n\n\nOur WDC offers you professional growth opportunity \n\nSpecializing in large, high-volume, custom treatment plant projects with advanced technologies, the Garver WDC is a knowledge-based hub that excels in producing highly technical, multidiscipline water and wastewater designs. Team member communication and coordination is constant, providing ample opportunity for your professional growth and a dynamic, fun work environment. \n\nGrow with Us  \nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.   \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work for Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.",
