    "jobId": "8a7887a199cae884019a01d28fc97eef",
    "title": "CAD (Civil 3D) Technician - Pipelines",
    "description": "CAD (Civil 3D) Technician - Pipelines \n          Greenville, South Carolina \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \n\nCAD (Civil 3D) Technician - Pipelines \n\n \n\nAs part of the Water Design Center (WDC) in Greenville, South Carolina, the CAD (Civil 3D) Technician - Pipelines will be responsible for developing civil engineering designs in support of various water/wastewater pipeline projects for Garvers Water Business Line.  Diversity in high-volume custom projects will allow this designer the opportunity to be hands-on with detailed design, collaborate with teams of designers and engineers and produce high-quality work in a rapidly growing business line.\n\n \n\nThe Civil Technician will provide civil engineering technical and design support as required for a variety of projects related primarily to developing pipeline corridor design plans and profiles. Other projects may include pump stations, lift stations, tanks, vaults, and other ancillary structures associated with water and sewer infrastructure projects as well as other civil engineering related projects.  The designer will be tasked with modeling, layout and profiling of piping networks and plans  using gravity and pressure networks with Civil 3D. Other tasks may include other site/civil related design work as assigned. The civil technician will be responsible for coordination with other support discipline activities, other designers and engineers, quantity estimating, and quality assurance and control.\n\n \n\nResponsibilities may include but not limited to:\n\n\n\tCoordination of survey services\n\tDeveloping detailed plans and details\n\tQuality program compliance: ensuring delivery of quality work products that adhere to Garver standardization.\n\tCivil standards and tools development, procurement, and training\n\n\nCandidates must have the ability to perform the following routine functions:\n\n\n\tAccurately complete drawings based on markups and detailed direction\n\tOrganizing drawing structures and files based on company standards\n\tAdhering to layering standards, line types, line widths, and plot styles\n\tGenerating plan and profile drawings complete with station numbering\n\tUtilizing gravity and pressure pipe networks\n\tDeveloping cross sections, Calculating volume and plan quantities\n\tReading and taking information from as-built drawings to develop existing condition models\n\tGenerating coordinates, boundary information, and survey information\n\tBeing consistent in design procedures across a variety of projects, producing record drawings\n\n\nAbout Garvers Greenville Water Design Center:\n\n \n\nThe Greenville Water Design Center is a knowledge-based hub that excels in highly technical, multi-discipline water and wastewater designs for locations all across the Garver footprint. The Greenville WDC specializes in large, high-volume, custom treatment plant projects with advanced technologies. Centralizing the location of the WDC means communication, coordination, and participation with team members is constant. This integral working relationship benefits the client through project delivery schedule and design quality, as well as the engineers opportunity for team collaboration and professional growth.\n\n \n\nRequirements:\n\n\n\tHigh school diploma\n\t4+ years experience with Civil 3D\n\n\nPreferred Skills:\n\n\n\tExperience using Autodesk software, including AutoCAD and Civil 3D\n\t2+ years experience in civil engineering design\n\tAssociates Degree in CAD or similar 2-year degree\n\tExperience with BIM file sharing software\n\tExperience using REVIT\n\tPrevious experience of designs, plans, and specifications for water and wastewater projects\n\tStrong knowledge base of engineering principals\n\tMust have strong communication skills (verbal and written)\n\tExperience using Bluebeam and MS Office products, including Word, Excel, Power Point, Project and Outlook\n\tStrong teaching and coaching skills to bring new team members up to speed\n\n\n\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance. \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,300 employees, Garver has a people-first culture that drives innovative, client-first service and is consistently recognized as a best firm to work for by Zweig Group. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com.  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law. \n\n \n\nLI-RK1",
