    "jobId": "8a7887a89f8b9426019f9067b94062dd",
    "title": "Civil Engineer",
    "description": "Civil Engineer \n          Greenville, South Carolina \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Are you a driven and experienced Civil Engineer looking to make a significant impact on water and wastewater treatment projects? Join our dynamic team and take on a rewarding role as our Civil Engineer, where youll have the chance to work on a wide range of projects, from designing new treatment facilities to improving existing infrastructure. Take this opportunity to showcase your expertise and contribute to the development of sustainable solutions that ensure clean water for communities. Not only will you have direct impact on the communities we serve but you will mentor the next generation of engineers within our Water Design Center.\n\n \n\nWhat youll do:\n\n\n\tCollaborate with multi-disciplinary teams, including civil, process, mechanical, structural, electrical, and I&C engineers, to deliver comprehensive and innovative designs that meet project objectives.\n\tCompleting civil designs including grading, paving, stormwater and yard piping routing and design for large, complex sites\n\tManage multiple projects concurrently, ensuring timely delivery, budget adherence, and exceptional quality of work products.\n\tActively mentor and develop junior team members, fostering their growth as design professionals and preparing them for increased responsibilities.\n\tEmbrace the opportunity for fieldwork and travel to support site assessments and provide construction support as needed.\n\n\nQualifications:\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil engineering from an ABET accredited program\n\t5 or more years of civil site design experience \n\tRegistered Professional Engineer (PE) strongly preferred\n\tStrong communication skills as required to manage project teams and maintain internal client relationships\n\tExperience with Autodesk software including AutoCAD and Civil 3D\n\tMust have a basic understanding of the multi-disciplined practices (i.e. process, surveying, geotechnical, structural, mechanical, electrical, instrumentation & control) required for the implementation of water/wastewater infrastructure improvements\n\tStrong teaching and coaching skills to mentor and communicate with team members of all levels\n\tPrevious experience as manager in charge of civil or related design, including detailed plans and specifications, for major water and wastewater treatment plant improvements projects\n\tExperience with land development in the private sector is preferred\n\n\nJoin our Water Design Center in Greenville and be at the forefront of site development design that contributes to clean water and sustainable development. Make a lasting impact as a Civil Engineer and bring your expertise to the forefront of water and wastewater treatment projects. Apply today and embark on an exciting journey with us!\n\n \n\nAbout Garvers Water Design Centers:\n\nThe Water Design Center (WDC) is a knowledge-based hub that excels in highly technical, multi- discipline water and wastewater designs. The WDC specializes in large, high-volume, custom treatment plant projects with advanced technologies. Centralizing the location of the WDC means communication, coordination, and participation with team members is constant. This integral working relationship benefits the client through project delivery schedule and design quality, as well as opportunity for team collaboration and professional growth.\n\n \n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n\n \n\nLI-ED1",
