    "jobId": "8a7883a89d9308df019dac1753d43378",
    "title": "Design and Visualization Technician",
    "description": "Design and Visualization Technician \n          Franklin, Tennessee \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Garvers Aviation team in Franklin, Tennessee seeks a Design and Visualization Technician to join our growing group of experienced engineers, designers, and technical writers.\n\n \n\nDo you enjoy working with creative teams to develop new and innovative solutions? As Garver Aviations design and visualization technician, you will join a team dedicated to advancing the way we communicate complex aviation designs for airports across the country. Responsibilities include developing conceptual design models and layouts for airport projects, including runways, taxiways, terminal construction, hangars, and more. This design and visualization technician would also be responsible for developing conceptual exhibits and graphic deliverables to assist in communicating complex design solutions in unique ways.\n\n \n\nFamiliarity with Autodesk platforms such as Civil 3D and Infraworks, along with knowledge of GIS software is a plus. The successful candidate will also understand basic system administration techniques as required to move data and files between applications and network locations and have a commitment to becoming a key member of a highly creative design team. Knowledge in the terminology, methods, practices and techniques of civil engineering and aviation planning and design, particularly site grading modeling and airspace modeling is preferred.\n\n \n\nRequirements\n\n\n\tHigh school diploma or GED\n\tStrong written and verbal communication skills\n\tHigh technological acumen\n\n\nPreferred Skills\n\n\n\tCertificate in Drafting with Experience with AutoCAD\n\tKnowledge in the terminology, methods, practices and techniques of airport design and planning and civil engineering; and ability to assist in other areas of our business as needed\n\tSkilled training (either formal or on-the-job) in Autodesks Civil 3D software packages, specifically in the site grading applications of either or both\n\tSkilled training (either formal or on-the job) in ArcGIS software\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n \n\nLI-VR1",
