    "jobId": "8a78859e9fd3bb25019ff1803894682c",
    "title": "Aviation Senior Site Civil Project Manager",
    "description": "Aviation Senior Site Civil Project Manager \n          Fort Worth, Texas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Aviation Senior Site Civil Project Manager\n\n \n\nFor the last six decades, Garver has been designing projects nationally for more than 250 aviation clients. Ranked 11 on the ENRs list of Top Airport Firms, Garver understands the complexities of airport systems held together by runways, roadways, facilities, and electrical systems that need to work in tandem to accommodate daily needs for travel and transport. As part of Garvers commitment to continued innovation in airport design, our Aviation Team is dedicated to providing the expertise and leadership to assist our clients in meeting both current and future needs nationally on large landside aviation projects.\n\n \n\nThe Aviation Senior Site Civil Project Manager will primarily be responsible for overseeing design teams and managing airport land development projects. The Aviation Senior Site Civil Project Manager must be able to work as a member of a multi-disciplined team, work with diverse clients, and produce complete design phase deliverables, including drawings, specifications, cost estimates, exhibits, technical reports, and narratives. Tasks associated with creating a set of construction documents include drafting, quantity computations, specifications, and cost estimates. Team coordination, project management, staff management, and project quality and financial performance management will also be expected. Past experience with design development software packages including AutoCAD, Civil 3D, and other civil design packages is required. \n\n \n\n Responsibilities will include\n\n\n\tOversee and manage a landside civil aviation project portfolio for Garver airports nationwide, with construction values reaching up to $100 million.\n\t Manage, mentor, and support a team of project engineers, fostering technical excellence and professional growth.\n\tOversee the financial performance and profitability of multiple projects, ensuring successful delivery within budget and schedule expectations.\n\tServe as a trusted advisor to clients while coordinating effectively with internal multidisciplinary teams, regulatory agencies, and external stakeholders.\n\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil engineering from an ABET-accredited program\n\tPE license\n\t10+ years of related experience with site civil design, permitting, applicable software applications\n\tManagement-level knowledge of AutoCAD Civil 3D\n\tDesign experience that includes drainage, grading, and utilities\n\tExperience with due diligence, permitting, and jurisdictional coordination\n\tExperience with task management, concept, design, and project management tasks\n\tManaging a multiple project portfolio\n\tEnsuring design teams adhere to project schedules, budgets and quality control plans\n\tStrong written and oral communication skills with both internal employees and external clients\n\tSome travel may be required (approximately 10% with occasional overnight)\n\n\n \n\nPreferred Skills\n\n\n\tAirport-related experience\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\n \n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com.\n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\nLI-VR1",
