    "title": "Structural Engineer",
    "description": "Structural Engineer \n          Houston, Texas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Overview\n\nAs a member of Garvers Buildings Team, the Structural Engineer will develop structural designs and documentation for various projects within the Buildings Business Line. Responsibilities include structural analysis, design, detailing, and construction administration for multiple structural systems, including:\n\n\n\tStructural Steel\n\tReinforced Concrete\n\tCold-Formed Steel\n\tReinforced masonry\n\tStructural Wood\n\n\nKey Responsibilities:\n\n\n\tConduct structural analysis, design, and detailing.\n\tPerform construction administration, including reviewing shop drawings, responding to RFIs, conducting site observations, and preparing reports.\n\tUtilize BIM design software to produce structural drawings.\n\tCoordinate with other disciplines.\n\tAssist project managers and follow QA/QC plans.\n\tManage multiple assignments concurrently.\n\tContinue education and learning based on project and team needs.\n\tMentor and train less experienced staff.\n\tAssign and coordinate tasks with engineers-in-training and BIM professionals.\n\tCollaborate with architects and contractors.\n\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\tMinimum of 3 years of professional structural engineering experience.\n\tStrong understanding of structural engineering principles.\n\tBachelors degree in civil engineering or architectural engineering with a structural emphasis from an ABET-accredited institution.\n\tLicensed Professional Engineer in Texas or ability to obtain licensure in Texas within 3 months of joining Garver.\n\tStrong understanding of structural engineering principles.\n\tExcellent oral and written communication skills.\n\tSelf-motivated and a good team player.\n\n\nPreferred Requirements and Skills\n\n\n\tMasters degree in civil engineering or architectural engineering with a structural emphasis from an ABET-accredited institution.\n\tProficient with Bentley RAM Structural System and RAM Elements.\n\tExperience with Autodesk Revit and Construction Cloud.\n\tProficiency with MS Office Suite.\n\tExperience with AIA MasterSpec.\n\tWorking knowledge of US building codes and structural design standards.\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.",
