    "jobId": "8a78839f9eb34c4a019ede05b75a4a77",
    "title": "Facilities Assessor",
    "description": "Facilities Assessor \n          Austin, Texas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Garver is seeking to add a Facilities Assessor to conduct BUILDER SMS inventories and assessments to help our defense clients remain mission ready.\n\n \n\nThe Federal Business Line is looking for a Facilities Assessor to join its growing team in Asset Management for its clients. Currently, the Federal Business Line uses BUILDER SMS for the majority of its clients. BUILDER SMS is an online database that comprises complexes, site, and buildings and their respective building components. These components are made of items in Architecture, Mechanical, Plumbing, Electrical, and Fire Protection. Federal completes field investigations at each site location assessing the buildings and then inputting and upkeeping the collected data within the BUILDER SMS databases for each client.\n\n \n\nQualifications\n\n\n\tBachelors degree\n\tAbility to become certified in BUILDER SMS within 6 months of hire date\n\tAbility to travel overnight up to 30%\n\tUnderstand a project work plan and execute based on a clients requirements\n\tAbility to assess multiple buildings within large complexes in a timely and detailed manner\n\tAbility to conduct services by abiding by safety precautions\n\tAble to produce quality work with minimal oversight\n\tProficient in written and oral communication skills according to skill requirements\n\tPossess strong computer skills, able to read, write, and comprehend written instructional documents\n\tWorking knowledge of how databases are created, formed, and upkept.\n\tAbility to calculate figures and amounts such as discounts, interest, commissions, proportions, percentages, area, circumference, and volume\n\tAbility to apply concepts of introductory algebra and geometry\n\tProlonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer\n\tProlonged periods of standing and walking within buildings\n\tOccasional periods of prolonged exposure to loud noises\n\tAbility to lift 25 pounds at times\n\tAbility to stand, walk, climb stairs, ladders, and reach with arms and hands as necessary\n\tAbility to hear and see to position and safety requirement levels\n\tOccasional exposure to elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, and chemicals\n\tMust be able to successfully pass an extensive background investigation\n\n\nResponsibilities\n\n\n\tWork in conjunction with the Federal Business Line to ensure the Builder SMS databases are kept current with condition assessments on facilities and other classifications as outlined in the Army BUILDER SMS Inventory and Assessment Guide\n\tPerform assessments on client facilities using professional expertise and judgment to determine physical condition and conformance with building codes and inspection criteria\n\tUpdate inspection and conditions results within BUILDER Sustainment Management System\n\t Produce reports and recommendations based on data captured in Sustainment Management Systems\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications:\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in engineering, architecture, construction management\n\tLicensure PE, EIT, Registered Architect, Asset Management\n\tWorking Knowledge of Building Construction and Maintenance\n\t0-5 years Technical Knowledge and field experience with BUILDER SMS\n\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n\n \n\nLI-CS1",
