    "jobId": "8a7885a89efb8776019f042c84d8303a",
    "title": "Civil Project Engineer",
    "description": "Civil Project Engineer \n          Frisco, Texas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Garver is seeking a Civil Project Engineer to join our growing Team in Frisco,TX to continue the tradition of providing quality service to our clients.\n\n \n\nResponsibilities in this position will include:\n\n\n\tCoordinating design with other disciplines and subconsultants.\n\tCommunicating with the project manager on deliverables, schedules, and budgets.\n\tPreparing design schematics in collaboration with environmental task leaders and other team members, consistent with the National Environmental Policy Act (NEPA).\n\tPreparing plans, specifications, cost estimates, reports, and calculations necessary for a complete deliverable package to the client.\n\tInteracting with the client, including preparing communications and other documentation.\n\tMentoring and training younger engineers on roadway design.\n\tServing as a Quality Assurance/Quality Control (QA/QC) Subject Matter Expert (SME) for reviewing deliverables.\n\tSupporting the Project Manager during Bid Phase and Construction including answering Requests for Information (RFI), reviewing project submittals from the contractor, preparing addenda and plan revisions.\n\tAssisting the Business Team Leader and Project Manager with marketing efforts, including proposal writing, client interaction, and public engagements.\n\n\nRequirements\n\n\n\tBachelor of Science degree in Civil Engineering or Civil Engineering Technology from an ABET accredited program.\n\tRegistered Professional Engineer (PE) in Texas or ability to obtain license through reciprocity.\n\tProfessional interpersonal and leadership skills, including a willingness to learn and be coached by a mentor.\n\tEffective written and verbal communication skills.\n\tFive (5) to ten (10) years of relevant site civil design experience \n\tAbility to lead a design team to meet a deliverable schedule within a defined budget\n\n\n\n\tMS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook) proficiency.\n\n\nPreferred Skills\n\n\n\tPrevious experience working with design software packages such as AutoCAD and Civil 3D\n\tBentley OpenRoads Designer proficiency.\n\tExperience in preparing fee proposal hour estimates.\n\n\n\n\nGrow With Us \n\n\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance. \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,300 employees, Garver has a people-first culture that drives innovative, client-first service and is consistently recognized as a best firm to work for by Zweig Group. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com.  \n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law. \n\n \n\nLI-EV1",
