    "jobId": "8a7883ac9f8b941b019fa4b81bb40e57",
    "title": "WI-MAP Project Engineer (Entry-Level)",
    "description": "WI-MAP Project Engineer (Entry-Level) \n          Austin, Texas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            Garver is seeking an entry level water industry professional to join the Water Infrastructure Modeling, Analytics, and Planning (WI-MAP) Team as a Project Engineer for our developing national resource team specializing in planning and conceptual evaluations for water, wastewater, and reuse infrastructure.\n\n \n\nThe successful candidate will be responsible for the management and execution of the technical components of exciting water industry projects. With an opportunity to join an established engineering consulting firm that is rapidly growing throughout the United States, the successful candidate will help execute water and wastewater infrastructure projects, provide limited support to regional teams with marketing and business development, participate in industry activities and events, and develop their career as part of a growing national resource team. Specifically, responsibilities will include a variety of projects related to one or more of the following categories: \n\n\n\t Water distribution systems, including hydraulic modeling, master planning, pumping and storage evaluations, water quality evaluations, and water loss studies; \n\tWastewater collection systems, including hydraulic modeling, master planning, rainfall-derived infiltration and inflow analyses, and lift station evaluations; \n\tWater supply and integrated master planning, including evaluations of surface water supplies, ground water supplies, reuse, and water rights; \n\tWater distribution and wastewater collection system asset management, including condition assessment, sanitary sewer evaluation studies, and capital planning; \n\tConveyance systems, including wire-to-water analysis, pumping optimization, and transient analysis \n\n\nResponsibilities will vary in relative volume, and change over time, but will generally include: \n\n\n\tProject Execution \n\tSupport conceptual planning studies as a Project Engineer \n\tEfficiently execute workload to maintain project schedule and project financials \n\tConsistently produce high-quality work products \n\tSupport development of materials for client workshops and present, as necessary, in client workshops \n\tCommunicate effectively with other WI-MAP staff at different office locations \n\tCoordinate with regional team client service managers and project managers \n\tCoordinate with Water Design Center personnel through design phases of projects \n\n\nQualified candidates must be capable of performing the following routine functions: \n\n\n\tDisplay technical competency of water / wastewater engineering and civil engineering commensurate with experience level in the profession \n\tContribute to multiple projects concurrently \n\tBe responsible for time management and work product quality \n\tComplete assigned scope items within the allotted budget and schedule \n\tConduct written and oral project reporting for project managers, regional team client service managers, the WI-MAP team leader, and clients, as necessary. Reporting will include project status, upcoming milestones, project accounting, percent completes, progress reports, etc. \n\tContribute to preparation and execution of Project Management Plans and Quality Control Plans \n\tSupport internal and external project workshops \n\n\nRequirements \n\n\n\tBachelors degree in civil or environmental engineering from an ABET accredited program \n\tStrong communication skills \n\n\nPreferred Skills \n\n\n\tMasters degree in civil or environmental engineering from an ABET accredited program \n\tRegistered as an Engineer-in-Training (EIT) or ability to become registered within six months of start of employment  \n\tExperience with hydraulic modeling software (e.g., Bentley WaterGEMS, Bentley SewerGEMS, Innovyze InfoWater, Innovyze InfoWorks ICM)  \n\tStrong technical background in hydraulics \n\tExperience with ESRI ArcGIS \n\tExperience with one of more of the main categories of work for the group outlined previously beyond university coursework \n\n\nGrow with Us  \nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.   \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work for Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.",
    "jobUrl": "https://garverusa.com/careers/jobdescription/Water/Texas/Austin/WI-MAP%20Project%20Engineer%20%28Entry-Level%29/?gnk=job&gni=8a7883ac9f8b941b019fa4b81bb40e57&d=detail",
