    "jobId": "8a78859e90a311600190a52e791953a4",
    "title": "Process Team Leader",
    "description": "Process Team Leader \n          College Station, Texas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nInterested in building, leading, and managing an integral group of engineering professionals in support of custom-designed water and wastewater treatment projects? Enjoy working on diverse, high-volume, exciting projects that give you the opportunity to be hands-on with design? Want to make a difference for communities in the heart of Texas and across the state?\n\nWeve got an opportunity for you here in our College Station Water Design Center (WDC).\n\nAs part of Garvers growing College Station WDC team, youll lead a team responsible for process design in support of water and wastewater treatment projects company wide. Youll evaluate, model, and design a wide variety of major process technologies for water and wastewater treatment projects. Youll be engaged in facility and equipment layouts, design calculations, coordinating with equipment vendors and regulatory agencies, coordinating support disciplines and regional offices, and performing quality reviews. Youll travel occasionally for business development purposes and when a project requires a site assessment as well as support during construction.\n\nWhat youll do:\n\n\n\tDesign water and wastewater treatment processes\n\tLead process modeling and develop design criteria using analysis of water and wastewater process modeling data\n\tLead water and wastewater process evaluation, selection, and implementation\n\tLead hydraulic analysis of water and wastewater treatment plants\n\tLead conceptual level designs for water and wastewater treatment systems\n\tLead detailed designs, including contract documents (plans and specifications)\n\tCoordinate with other support discipline activities, regional Garver offices, and regulatory and funding agencies\n\tSupport regional teams with treatment related business development activities\n\tDevelop scope, schedule, level of effort, and fees for projects\n\tPlan and monitor budgets\n\tEnsure quality program compliance and delivery of work products that adhere to Garver standardization\n\tManage and mentor teams\n\n\nWhat youll bring:\n\n\n\tMasters degree in civil, environmental, chemical, or related engineering discipline from an ABET accredited program\n\tProfessional Engineer Licensure (PE)\n\t10 or more years of direct design experience with municipal water and wastewater facilities\n\tTwo or more years of experience leading project teams\n\tExperience with process modeling software such as Hydromatis GPS-X, Dynamita Sumo, and EnviroSim BioWin\n\tExperience overseeing process designs, including detailed plans and specifications for major projects\n\tUnderstanding of water and wastewater treatment plant systems in a facility-wide environment\n\tExperience performing process equipment evaluation, sizing, and cost estimating\n\tExperience with hydraulic modeling software\n\n\nBonus points if you bring these, too:\n\n\n\tProfessional Engineer Licensure (PE) in several states, including TX, OK, NM, AZ, CO\n\t15 years or more of experience with municipal water and wastewater process related design\n\tFive or more years of experience leading project teams\n\tRelationships with municipal clients in Garvers footprint\n\tA record of active participation in professional organizations such as AWWA, WEF, WRF\n\n\nOur WDC offers you professional growth opportunity\n\nSpecializing in large, high-volume, custom treatment plant projects with advanced technologies, the Garver WDC is a knowledge-based hub that excels in producing highly technical, multidiscipline water and wastewater designs. Team member communication and coordination is constant, providing ample opportunity for your professional growth and a dynamic, fun work environment.\n\nBenefits & Perks\n\nGarvers is committed to providing the best employee experience, and because we are a firm made up of engineers and designers who love data, we made that commitment measurable. Every year we ensure our benefits remain in the top quartile of our industry. What does that mean for you? Paid parental leave, 401k match, contributions to your HSA, paid health and dental insurance premiums for employees enrolled in our nationally recognized Wellness Program, gym membership reimbursements, tuition reimbursements, and much, much more.\n\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n\n \n\nLI-CP1",
