    "jobId": "8a7887ac9c2fd12b019c58a39ab663f1",
    "title": "Water Modeling & Planning Squad Leader",
    "description": "Water Modeling & Planning Squad Leader \n          Frisco, Texas \n        \n      \n  \n  \n\n  \n    \n            \nGarver is seeking a Texas Squad Leader for its Water Infrastructure  Modeling, Analytics and Planning (WI-MAP) Team. The Squad Leader supervises a team of engineers and project managers engaged in the delivery of water, wastewater, stormwater and reuse modeling and planning projects across Texas. Provides daily oversight, technical guidance, and leadership to staff executing projects involving hydraulic modeling, master planning, data analysis and infrastructure evaluations. Supports staff development and project excellence by coordinating resources, reviewing technical work, and ensuring alignment with project goals, quality standards, and client priorities. Reports directly to the WI-MAP Practice Area Leader, and functions as part of the WI-MAP Leadership Team.\n\nThis Texas Squad Leader can be located in the Fort Worth, Dallas, Austin, San Antonio, or Houston metro areas.\n\n \n\nEssential Functions\n\n\n\tSupervise and support a team of engineers and project managers.\n\tProvide technical guidance and review for modeling, planning, data analysis and infrastructure evaluation projects.\n\tMonitor workload and assign project responsibilities to ensure appropriate staff utilization.\n\tSupport the development of scopes, schedules, budgets, and staffing plans for planning-phase projects.\n\tEnsure high-quality and timely delivery of water, wastewater and stormwater master plans, hydraulic models, and design support studies.\n\tFacilitate knowledge sharing, mentoring, and technical training opportunities for team members.\n\tCoordinate across departments to support seamless transitions from planning to design phases.\n\tContribute to the preparation and quality control of proposals and planning deliverables.\n\tReview project metrics (budget, schedule, performance) and provide updates to leadership on a routine basis.\n\tParticipate in internal quality assurance reviews and support the implementation of best practices.\n\tIdentify resource needs, support recruitment or onboarding of new team members and support overall team development.\n\n\n \n\nEducation, Experience, and License Requirements\n\n\n\tBachelors degree in Civil, Environmental, or a related field of study from an ABET-accredited program.\n\tLicensed Professional Engineer (PE).\n\tMinimum of 8+ years of experience in water/wastewater/stormwater infrastructure planning, including at least 2 years in master planning or hydraulic modeling.\n\tAt least 2 years of experience mentoring and/or supervising engineering or technical staff.\n\n\n \n\nKnowledge, Skills, and Abilities\n\n\n\tStrong understanding of water distribution, wastewater collection, and stormwater system planning and modeling.\n\tFamiliarity with a range of hydraulic modeling software, including Autodesk InfoWater Pro and InfoWorks ICM, Bentley WaterGEMS and SewerGEMS, and others.\n\tWorking knowledge of infrastructure design and capital improvement planning principles.\n\tAbility to lead and develop high-performing teams in a collaborative environment.\n\tExcellent verbal and written communication skills for both technical and non-technical audiences.\n\tProficient in managing multiple projects and deadlines with a focus on quality and efficiency.\n\tAbility to interpret, review, and contribute to scopes of work, proposals, and technical reports.\n\tSkilled in performance management, feedback, and mentoring of staff.\n\tStrong problem-solving skills and commitment to client satisfaction.\n\n\nGrow With Us\n\nGarver offers its employees programs such as company-paid professional memberships, company support for industry licenses and continuing education opportunities that foster a progressive atmosphere. Garver provides the tools, resources, and environment to develop leaders, stimulate ideas, and accomplish projects. By offering highly competitive salary packages, attractive benefits, and a comprehensive wellness program; Garver walks the talk when it comes to work-life balance.\n\n \n\nFounded in 1919, Garver is an employee-owned engineering, planning, and environmental services firm focused on aviation, transportation, buildings, federal, water and wastewater services; surveying; advisory services; and construction engineering and inspection. In the top 100 of Engineering News-Records Top 500 Design Firms list, with more than 1,400 employees, Garver provides an exceptional level of client service that reflects our people-first culture, which has achieved Zweig Group Best Firm to Work For Legacy Status. Learn how Garver invests in people and places they call home at GarverUSA.com. \n\n \n\nGarver is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all applicants and employees. Our employment practices are based upon an individuals capabilities and qualifications without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.\n\n \n\nLI-ED1",
